  "notes": "This contract records the portable C++ TCK check and focused pure-Java parity for mixed ordinary attribute ownership queries. The sources use only the official IEEE RTIambassador and FederateAmbassador APIs plus their language standard libraries; adapters supply the provider package, two-attribute FOM, endpoint, and callback configuration. They verify exact owned and unowned attribute partitions and suppression of ownership-query results that have not crossed the callback boundary when the object is removed. The broader Java invalid-object/attribute scenario stays independent and currently fails on the provider's wrapped exception; no negative failure is suppressed or mapped as a normative claim. Callback order, private registries, interoperability, and conformance are not asserted.",
